- For \(p\ge5\), the paper directly constructs \(\{u,v\},\{uv^2,uv^4\}\) using four group multiplications.
- Structure-aware random guessing succeeds with probability at least \(1/20\), versus the required \(<10^{-6}\).
- For \(p=3\), the theorem’s sufficient \(z,t\) choices have density at least \(4/9\).
- Consequently, neither quotient depth nor relabelling creates hardness; the search remains in \(\mathbb F_p^2\).

The complete quantitative analysis is in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1604.06031/REJECTED.md). Per the task instructions, no generator or fabricated gate/oracle artifacts were produced after the analytical failure.
